{"archetypes":[{"name":"label-sweep","focus_area":"correctness","weight":1,"rationale":"Doc+rename changes risk leaving stale occurrences of the old label in files the plan did not enumerate; a targeted sweep catches missed rename sites before CI.","prompt_body":"Grep the full repository for every occurrence of the string 'Show latest design proposal' and the old Gate C bold-note phrase 'pick \"Other\"' to verify the plan's five-file list is exhaustive. Check whether any files outside those five — such as other skills, docs, README, or larch-logs entries that are actively read at runtime — carry instances that would need updating or a freeze note. Verify that the new label 'See full plan' appears in every location the plan claims to introduce it and in no location the plan does not claim to touch. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"option-arithmetic","focus_area":"correctness","weight":1,"rationale":"The plan introduces a 4/3/2-option state machine across Gate C and Gate A; arithmetic inconsistencies between SKILL.md and approval-gates.md prose are a common doc-drift defect in multi-file rename changes.","prompt_body":"Trace every description of option counts across SKILL.md and approval-gates.md: below-cap Gate C initial (should be 4), at-cap Gate C initial (should be 3), after See-full-plan pick below cap (should be 3), after See-full-plan pick at cap (should be 2), Gate A Shape 2 initial (should be 3), and Gate A Shape 2 after See-full-plan pick (should be 2). Flag any prose location where the implied count differs from the plan's stated arithmetic. Also check whether the per-tier cap paragraph at the top of approval-gates.md is updated to describe the new 3-option at-cap list as the plan claims. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"test-pin-completeness","focus_area":"architecture","weight":1,"rationale":"The plan adds one new approval-gates.md assertion and updates two existing ones; verifying that every new behavioral contract has a pinning assertion catches coverage gaps the plan may have omitted from its testing strategy section.","prompt_body":"Read test-design-structure.sh and test-emit-design-plan-preview.sh to verify that every new literal string the plan introduces is covered by at least one contains or grep assertion: the four-option Gate C prose in SKILL.md, the cap-omission three-option prose in SKILL.md, the 'See full plan' token in the approval-gates.md Gate C section, and the updated bold-note text in emit-design-plan-preview.sh. Check whether the Other-path backward-compat paragraph — which the plan says is preserved but unchanged in both SKILL.md and approval-gates.md — is pinned by any assertion, since an unpinned preserved section can silently drift. Flag any new contract prose that has no corresponding test assertion and any old assertion that the plan claims to update but whose updated literal does not appear in the test file. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."}]}
